# Mirror of the root .dockerignore for service/Dockerfile builds.
# Docker reads .dockerignore only from the build-context root, and the
# documented build uses the repository root as context
# (`docker build -f service/Dockerfile .`), so the root file is the one
# that actually excludes files. This copy is inert for that build; it
# exists so the two files' patterns can be kept in sync by eye, and it
# applies if anyone builds with service/ as the context (which the
# Dockerfile's COPY paths reject). Keep the nested `**` forms below in
# sync with the root file: a bare `*.db` matches only at the context
# root, which is how a nested database copy once re-entered the context.
.git
.venv
.venv-fuzz
dist
build
.gitignore
.github
Makefile
MANIFEST.in
pyproject.toml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.gitattributes
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.hypothesis
**.hypothesis
.scratch
docs
tests
fuzzers
benchmarks
*.db
**.db
*.db-wal
**.db-wal
*.db-shm
**.db-shm
*.duckdb
**.duckdb
*.duckdb-wal
**.duckdb-wal
*.sqlite3
**.sqlite3
